``` SUCI flood (DoS against the home network)
    Many SUCIs that can't be decrypted, from the same cell, very fast.
    The home network never learns who sent them, so there is no
    subscriber to count. Instead we count how many per minute per cell.
    Normal traffic almost never has SUCI_INVALID.
    Threshold: 10 per cell per minute. ```
index=fiveg source="traffic.jsonl" event_type=auth_failure cause=SUCI_INVALID
| bin _time span=1m
| stats count by _time cell
| where count >= 10
